Z||000000||David DeVoe||11-21-2001||08:28 AM||||Whats this P 22 I keep seeing usually in discussions about Fiero parts. <BR>Dave||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||11-21-2001||08:46 AM||||It is a GM book that shows all the parts and part numbers of everything on a Fiero. It has illustrations of all parts needed for a particular assembly. They have numbers next to the drawing of the part and these reference the GM part number. Many of the newer cars have them on CD so the parts department at a dealer can just use a computer instead of paging thru books. <BR>P22 is strictly Fiero's.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||11-21-2001||08:49 AM||||Is the P22 available on CD? ||||reg||5
Z||000003||Oreif||11-21-2001||08:57 AM||||Yes, recently some one has been making them on CD. Here is an Ebay link: (the auction has ended but you can see if they have more)<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=597992899&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=597992899&r=0&t=0</A> <P>He has a lot of others for sale of different cars, You could E-mail him and see if he has more Fiero ones.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||pherder||11-21-2001||09:39 AM||||Two nit picking things I have to say ...<P>One, it is a <BR>1984-88 <BR>PONTIAC <BR>P <BR>PARTS AND ILLUSTRATION CATALOG<BR><FONT SIZE="1">EFFECTIVE NOVEMBER 90 GENERAL MOTORS CORPORATION <B>22P</B></FONT><P>Second, I have one of those CDs and it is a scanned in copy of this <B>22P</B> book BUT only the second half of the book.<P>The scanned in pictures are okay but the scanned in part numbers are very hard to read.  As you zoom in on them, they tend to blur out making them unreadable.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>But I will have to say, it is better than nothing!<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000005||watts||11-21-2001||12:21 PM||||I found the same (?) CD for auction over at Yahoo for a bit less than half!   <BR> <A HREF="http://page.auctions.shopping.yahoo.com/auction/57399321" TARGET=_blank>http://page.auctions.shopping.yahoo.com/auction/57399321</A> <P>Is this worth getting pherder?  If it's only half the book, what's missing?  Are the parts indexed or anything (like some searchable PDF's are)?  Are the pictures clear when printed?<P>I'd like to get one of these, but only if it's not just some useless crap.<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||pherder||11-21-2001||12:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by watts:<BR><B>I found the same (?) CD for auction over at Yahoo for a bit less than half!   <BR> <A HREF="http://page.auctions.shopping.yahoo.com/auction/57399321" TARGET=_blank>http://page.auctions.shopping.yahoo.com/auction/57399321</A> <P>Is this worth getting pherder?  If it's only half the book, what's missing?  Are the parts indexed or anything (like some searchable PDF's are)?  Are the pictures clear when printed?<P>I'd like to get one of these, but only if it's not just some useless crap.<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>It is worth the ~$20 listed on Yahoo ... it is the same seller (at least from the same city!)<P>The 22P has two sections, the first is everything is listed by group number.  The second is the illustration /exploded view listings.<P>I find the group section handy when I can find a part illustration of something like the part I want but the part I really want is not pictured.  I go to the group section and there are parts listed there that aren't in the pictures.  It also lists the 1990 list price of the part and the page numbers (if available) of an illustration of the part in case it is pictured somewhere else.<P>The second section (exploded view section) is what is included on the CD.<P>I have copied the PDF file to my HD (20 MB!) and I do use it for a quick look up but usually I end up dragging out the paper book to get the exact part numbers.<P>I wish I had found the Yahoo auction for ~$20 instead of the ~$50 I ended up spending for mine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000007||scotkb75||11-22-2001||11:16 PM||||I agree with the worth of the $50 CD, better than nothing but not close to a complete book.  When I save enough $$, I will be back in the hunt for a complete factory book.||||reg||1
